In article <1993Aug20.091843.1@vxdesy.desy.de> pawlak@vxdesy.desy.de writes:
>It wasn't a level, it was just that three stooges appearing as monster 
>type. It was definitely in 2.3, possibly also in late (unofficial?) 2.2
>versions. It went away when 3.0 came and removed many 'modern' things
>(hand grenades, pizza slices, police badges etc). Interesting that they
>left tourists and expensive cameras in through...

Just a historical note....

The stooges were removed, not because they were just modern, but because
they got in your way while being impossible to kill.  Even the people in the
devteam who liked modern things (which after all games like Zork arew
positively loaded with) couldn't stand the Stooges.

Badges were totally worthless, which is why they went.  (I rejoined the devteam
just in time to see badges get deleted without hearing any of the discussion.)

Pizza slices were a hack I put in when I wanted a fruit and Nethack didn't
have one.  They're not really _gone_, they're changed to real fruits, and if
you don't define TUTTI_FRUTTI you get slices of pizza instead.

I've never seen a version with grenades in them, and I think they (and the
light sabers) were released as a separate patch, not with 2.2 or 2.3....
